        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "I encountered this too, and noticed few things which make it show up again, and this is the easiest if it happened:\n\n### Press ctrl-G (or right-click -> \"goto current date\").\nThis reloads the history at the current date, which is the bottom of the history, and makes it show up again. As usual, scrolling up will show older history.\n\nOther things which work but are less easy or less fun:\n- Right-click -> \"load chat history\" (2nd item from the bottom) and click \"OK\" to load today's history (seems same as ctrl-G, just with two mouse clicks).\n- Search the history (ctrl-F or right-click -> \"search in text\") and type something which is found (one letter is enough).\n- Send a message.\n- Log out and log in again.\n\nFor me the issue seems to happen if I scroll up so that it fetches a bit more history from the disk/database into the window, then scroll back down to the bottom - and then suddenly it fetches the maximum allowed history size from the disk/database (the scrollbar becomes small), and then close and open the window.\n\nIf I don't scroll up to fetch more history then the issue doesn't happen to me.\n\nEither way, ctrl-G always seem to make it normal again (and only a small portion of the history is loaded at the window, and the scrollbar is relatively big).\n",
            "created_at": "2025-08-06T23:03:03Z",
